WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.868 line:92%
-16th. You just had your 16th season premiere at "SNL."

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.300 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-It's unbelievable, man.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.234 line:92%
Like, I'm the record holder... -You are the record holder.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:08.734 line:92%
-...of "Saturday Night Live"... [ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.100 line:92%
-When -- Yeah. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.667 line:92%
Deservedly so. -Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:15.567 line:92%
-Did you enjoy the first show back?

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:16.934 line:92%
Season premieres are always exciting.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.868 line:92%
-I enjoyed watching it. I sure did.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.033 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. -Yeah.

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:21.534 line:92%
I was not in it much, so... -Yeah.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:24.334 line:92%
-Yeah. It was all good, though. I did my part in the monologue

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.133 line:92%
and I got to watch the circus unfold.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.033 line:92%
-There was a circus on Saturday. -Yeah.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.901 line:92%
-A Kanye West-led circus. -Yeah.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.534 line:92%
-Particularly at the end of the show, now he --

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:34.701 line:92%
For those who didn't watch,

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.434 line:92%
he did a song at the end of the show.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:37.968 line:92%
Then the show ended. -Yeah.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:40.434 line:92%
-But then it turned out that he brought a bunch of people on --

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:41.767 line:92%
He brought the cast back on stage...

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:42.934 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:45.300 line:92%
-While he gave a very political speech.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.534 line:92%
-Yeah, he voiced his opinion very loudly. Yeah.

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:49.534 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah. -For a long time.

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.067 line:92%
-Not a guy who's scared of his opinion and voicing it.

00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:52.234 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-No, no, not at all.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:54.100 line:92%
And, you know, we're all entitled to our opinion.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.434 line:92%
-Sure. -I don't know if that's

00:00:55.434 --> 00:00:57.267 line:92%
the moment necessarily to hold people hostage like that.

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.968 line:92%
[ Laughter ] But, hey, you know...

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.000 line:92%
-Well, the thing about what -- I, you know, when I share

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.968 line:92%
my opinion, one thing I try not to do is say,

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:04.167 line:92%
"Come on, everyone. Come on up."

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.567 line:92%
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. -"Come join me."

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.300 line:92%
-Yeah. "Come into the wolf's den, and then I'll --"

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.901 line:92%
-"You guys, you all disagree with me, right? Come up here."

00:01:10.901 --> 00:01:12.734 line:92%
-"Yeah. Yeah, come up here." -"Join me while I do this."

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:14.200 line:92%
-"I'll be nice, I promise."

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.868 line:92%
-"I promise I'll be nice." -"Get up here." Yeah, and then--

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:19.067 line:92%
-"I'm lying." -Proceeds to caca on people.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.834 line:92%
Yeah, that's what he did. -You were not --

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:25.267 line:92%
Because people, again, it was not...it was not on broadcast.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.601 line:92%
Some people filmed it. -Right.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:27.767 line:92%
-You were not on stage, I noticed.

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.534 line:92%
-Yeah, I had departed. -Okay.

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.200 line:92%
-Yes. -Now, was that a choice?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.701 line:92%
Did you chose to depart or you just departed by --

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:35.634 line:92%
-I mean, I was just, you know, thinking that, you know,

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:36.968 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I would rather, like,

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.634 line:92%
watch the, you know, performance on TV.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.467 line:92%
Sometimes I like watching the musical performance...

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.000 line:92%
-Of course. -...how everyone would see it,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.167 size:88% position:44% line:92%
like, on TV as a viewer.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.701 line:92%
And so then, when you saw what happened,

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.367 line:92%
were you so happy with the choice you'd made?

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.634 line:92%
-For sure. Yes. -[ Laughs ]

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:53.534 line:92%
-As soon as he said, "Hey, join me up on stage, everybody,"

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:55.667 line:92%
I was like, "Oh, there goes the little cheese

00:01:55.667 --> 00:01:58.334 line:92%
in the mouse trap." [ Laughter ]

00:01:58.334 --> 00:01:59.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"It's going down."

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:03.100 line:92%
I felt so bad for those guys, because it's hard to stand there

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.868 line:92%
and not be able to, you know,

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.734 line:92%
debate somebody who's going to so far

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.934 line:92%
against, you know, your personal opinion as well,

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.634 line:92%
and just stand there and take it. Just, you know...

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:13.234 line:92%
-And, you know, the other thing is, I think that --

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.200 line:92%
and you and I can both speak to this, at "SNL,"

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.868 line:92%
you try make the people that are the musical guests, the hosts,

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.033 line:92%
you try to make them comfortable.

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.601 line:92%
-We're fair. Yeah, we're fair.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:22.334 line:92%
We're in the service business. You know what I mean?

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.334 line:92%
We try to cater to the host, make sure they have a good show

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.000 line:92%
and whatnot. And then, you know,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.234 line:92%
when musical guests come in, and they're a little bit crazy,

00:02:28.234 --> 00:02:29.434 line:92%
maybe they're a little bit crazy.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:30.634 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughter ]

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:31.934 line:92%
-We let 'em have that. -Yeah.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.000 line:92%
-I mean, but we don't judge. -Absolutely.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.734 line:92%
-We're not there to judge.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.167 line:92%
-I had one of the most delightful things happen to me

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.100 line:92%
on the street the other day. I was walking down the street.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.033 line:92%
I bumped into you and your baby girl Gianna.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:43.133 line:92%
-Yeah. On Super Daddy duty. That's right.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:44.300 line:92%
-Super Daddy duty. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.734 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, that's right.

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:47.067 line:92%
-Oh! -There she is. Look at her.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.634 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Babbles ]

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:53.501 line:92%
-So first of all, it's not 'cause you are --

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.467 line:92%
you turned 40 this year. -Yes.

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:56.801 line:92%
-You had your second little girl.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:58.601 line:92%
-Greatest summer of my entire life.

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.634 line:92%
My second little girl was born. She's healthy. She's happy.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.300 line:92%
My wife is healthy and happy.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.534 line:92%
My big girl, Georgia, is healthy and happy.

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:07.868 line:92%
She's 4. She's obsessed with her sister.

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:10.000 line:92%
We got nominated and won an Emmy.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.334 line:92%
-You won an Emmy. -The show won an Emmy.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.901 line:92%
I got personally nominated. [ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:15.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right. You, um...

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.400 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You won a, uh... -Crazy.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.968 line:92%
-We won an Emmy. -You won an Emmy for this song?

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:21.901 line:92%
-Yes. Thank you. Shout-out.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.901 line:92%
We shout-out K-Ci and JoJo all the time

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.234 line:92%
because they were heavy inspirations for that.

00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:28.701 line:92%
-And that is -- You wrote a song with Chance the Rapper.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.767 line:92%
-Yeah, man. Shout-out to Chance the Rapper, man.

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:33.100 line:92%
Once again, I got nominated the first time with Chance, so...

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.601 line:92%
-Yeah. -...the dude is brilliant.

00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.701 line:92%
-Well, I -- you and I came by our Emmys in very similar ways,

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:37.868 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which is, I won an Emmy

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:39.167 line:92%
for writing a song with Justin Timberlake.

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.300 line:92%
And I think the key is -- -Gotta pick a good horse.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.367 line:92%
-Yeah, exactly. -Gotta pick a good horse.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.801 line:92%
-No one, I feel like, is looking at

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:47.868 line:92%
the ballot, being like, "Oh, I like Kenan Thompson's song."

00:03:47.868 --> 00:03:49.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly. No.

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:52.367 line:92%
I picked two good horses -- Chance and Chris Redd.

00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:53.901 line:92%
-Chris Redd, absolutely. -Chris Redd is dynamite.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:57.501 line:92%
-He's fantastic. And what is it? Is it Chris' second season now?

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.300 line:92%
-Yeah, man. The boy's blowing up. He's already got an Emmy.

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.801 line:92%
-Very excited. Yeah. He's doing a great job.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.701 line:92%
-Unbelievable. -You -- you're very --

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:04.133 line:92%
It was both -- it was bittersweet,

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:06.868 line:92%
'cause you were nominated for supporting actor, you lost.

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:08.767 line:92%
With that said, Henry Winkler won.

00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:09.868 line:92%
-That's what I'm saying, like... -Yeah.

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:11.767 line:92%
-If there's anybody to lose to...

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.234 line:92%
-It's Henry Winkler. -...it's Henry.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:15.901 line:92%
I mean, he was sitting right across the aisle from me. Yeah.

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.133 line:92%
-Yeah, give it up for Henry Winkler.

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:20.000 line:92%
-Seriously, like... [ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.167 size:88% position:44% line:92%
His story is incredible.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:23.767 line:92%
He waited 42 years for that Emmy.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.033 line:92%
-Yeah. -You know what I mean?

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.300 line:92%
He was nominated. -In the theater the whole time.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.801 line:92%
-Yeah. Right. Just sitting there that entire --

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:29.934 line:92%
just ready. Speech written, getting dusty.

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:32.100 line:92%
-Changing it, as it was. -Rewrites.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.601 line:92%
-He has new kids. Has to like -- -Oh, my God. But, yeah.

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.667 line:92%
I mean, he sat right across the aisle from me.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:40.634 line:92%
And when I saw him, you know, I gave him, you know,

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.634 line:92%
like, a nice across the aisle squeeze...

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.300 line:92%
-Yeah. -...because he's a dear friend.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:48.601 line:92%
We worked on a show, an animated show called "Sit Down, Shut Up,"

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.467 line:92%
and we were, like, faculty members or whatever.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:53.434 line:92%
And when I first met him, he was the sweetest,

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:55.934 line:92%
little old Jewish man that I've ever seen in my life.

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:58.667 line:92%
He was like a sweet little Jewish gumdrop.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:01.067 line:92%
You just want to, like, eat him up.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.133 line:92%
And he, like, just gave me a hug. And he's so warm.

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:04.567 line:92%
And we talked. And I was just like,

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.868 line:92%
"I can't believe I'm talking to Fonzarelli right now."

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:08.200 line:92%
You know what I mean? -Yeah.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.534 line:92%
-He's talking to me like he knows me.

00:05:09.534 --> 00:05:10.868 line:92%
He's like, "We watch you all the time.

00:05:10.868 --> 00:05:12.667 line:92%
We love you in the Winkler house."

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:15.501 line:92%
And then we were nominated in the same category.

00:05:15.501 --> 00:05:17.934 line:92%
And, like, that's just a flattery in its own right.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:19.133 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.868 line:92%
Just to be in the same sentence as that guy.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:23.367 line:92%
And he won. And it stung. You know?

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:25.434 line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ] -But, um... [ Laughs ]

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:28.033 line:92%
I was so happy for him because I know how great he is.

00:05:28.033 --> 00:05:30.133 line:92%
And then I found out about, you know, the 42-year thing.

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.200 line:92%
And I was like, "Well, yeah, of course he should have won."

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.367 line:92%
-Yeah. -You know what I mean?

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:35.267 line:92%
And then I said something nice to him

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:37.734 line:92%
when I presented the award myself at the end of the night,

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:39.000 line:92%
just because it came from the heart.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.801 line:92%
And I saw him sitting there. I congratulated him.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:42.734 line:92%
And he wrote me a letter. -That's so amazing.

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.067 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-He sent me a letter.

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:45.300 line:92%
Like, wrote me, like, a thank you letter.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.934 line:92%
-He's truly the nicest. -He's a sweet, sweet man.

00:05:46.934 --> 00:05:49.000 line:92%
It's one of those people, it would be so devastating

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.467 line:92%
if you met Henry Winkler, and he wasn't the nicest person.

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:54.067 line:92%
And he just -- -Ohh. It would suck so hard.

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:55.567 line:92%
-It would suck so hard. [ Laughter ]

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.667 line:92%
-Because, like, I could get it, like, if he was just The Fonz.

00:05:57.667 --> 00:05:59.801 line:92%
I was like, "Yeah, okay, he's kind of a tough guy."

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:01.167 line:92%
But he also played, like, you know,

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:03.601 line:92%
a lot of really sweet teachers. -Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:03.601 --> 00:06:05.901 line:92%
-And, like, a lot of good dads and stuff like that.

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:07.734 line:92%
Especially in "Click." You know, Adam Sandler's dad.

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.234 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Oh, my God. So sweet.

